Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD=3 holds only the writes that went to copied pages, and claims them at once

0496 held every guest write collected while a guard was up. But the caches rely on collected
writes being applied soon: applying one first takes it out of the GPU-written ranges, which is
what keeps a fence or read download from landing the GPU's older bytes over it. EDEN_NX2_OVERWRITE_CHECK
saw guest writes over GPU-written ranges not yet landed in 10-20% of frames. Held for a frame,
those would be overwritten in guest memory.

Now a gather made while a guard is up keeps back only the writes that went to a page with a
copy (so: made after the present, to a page the frame in flight reads), takes them out of the
GPU-written ranges at once (RasterizerInterface::ClaimCpuWrites, what OnCacheInvalidations does
first) and applies them at the first gather after the guard is lifted. Every other write is
applied as before, so traffic between the game and the GPU on other pages is untouched.

---
diff --git a/src/video_core/ahead_guard.h b/src/video_core/ahead_guard.h
index 5f22167..21048d9 100644
--- a/src/video_core/ahead_guard.h
+++ b/src/video_core/ahead_guard.h
@@ -44,15 +44,17 @@
 ///      (TakeRedirty), so a buffer uploaded from a copy is uploaded again from memory. With the
 ///      pool full a write waits as with =1.
 ///
-///   =3 (copy and hold): as =2, and the guest writes the cores collect while a guard is up stay
-///      with them until it is lifted (GPU::GatherAndApply gathers nothing meanwhile); those made
-///      before the present are gathered at the present (GPU::GatherForAheadGuard) and applied
-///      as usual. T89, batch t89-a: with =2 a write made after the present was still applied
-///      in the middle of the frame in flight. For most pages that only marks them for an upload,
-///      which then reads the copy; but a write into memory the GPU owns is uploaded into the host
-///      buffer at once (BufferCache's inline page writes), and a texture the write touches is
-///      uploaded again from memory. Two small dark glitches and a fade out of order stayed, and
-///      eleven moments with EDEN_UP_AHEAD_ALWAYS.
+///   =3 (copy and hold): as =2, and a guest write collected while a guard is up that went to a
+///      copied page (so: made after the present, to a page the frame in flight reads) is applied
+///      only after the guard is lifted (GPU::GatherAndApply). It leaves the GPU-written ranges
+///      at once, so no download lands over it meanwhile. The writes made before the present are
+///      gathered at the present (GPU::GatherForAheadGuard) and applied as usual, and so is every
+///      write to a page without a copy. T89, batch t89-a: with =2 a write made after the present
+///      was still applied in the middle of the frame in flight. For most pages that only marks
+///      them for an upload, which then reads the copy; but a write into memory the GPU owns is
+///      uploaded into the host buffer at once (BufferCache's inline page writes), and a texture
+///      the write touches is uploaded again from memory. One or two small dark glitches and a
+///      fade out of order stayed, and nine moments with EDEN_UP_AHEAD_ALWAYS.
 ///
 ///   EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_SETS=<mask>   which finished frames' pages are guarded, bit d = the frame
 ///                                     d presents back (default 14: one, two and three back;
@@ -461,11 +463,28 @@ inline bool Active() {
     return Enabled() && Get().active.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
 }
 
-/// =3: a guard is up, so the guest writes collected now are a later frame's and stay with their
-/// cores until it is lifted (GPU::GatherAndApply).
+/// =3: a guard is up, so a guest write collected now that went to a copied page is a later
+/// frame's and is applied after the guard is lifted (GPU::GatherAndApply).
 inline bool HoldWrites() {
     return Mode() == 3 && Get().active.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
 }
+
+/// Whether a page of [device_addr, device_addr + size) has a copy now: a guest thread wrote it
+/// after the present of the frame in flight. Lock-free.
+inline bool HasCopy(u64 device_addr, u64 size) {
+    constexpr u64 limit = u64{1} << AddressBits;
+    if (size == 0 || device_addr >= limit) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    State& s = Get();
+    const u64 last = ((std::min)(device_addr + size, limit) - 1) >> PageBits;
+    for (u64 page = device_addr >> PageBits; page <= last; ++page) {
+        if ((s.copied[page / 64].load(std::memory_order_acquire) & (u64{1} << (page % 64))) != 0) {
+            return true;
+        }
+    }
+    return false;
+}
 inline bool Guarded(u64 device_addr, u64 size) {
     constexpr u64 limit = u64{1} << AddressBits;
     if (size == 0 || device_addr >= limit) {
diff --git a/src/video_core/gpu.cpp b/src/video_core/gpu.cpp
index bb8c30b..b5781fc 100644
--- a/src/video_core/gpu.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/gpu.cpp
@@ -189,9 +189,10 @@ struct GPU::Impl {
     ///      so buffers uploaded from the copies are uploaded again;
     ///  =3: first the writes gathered at the present that put the guard up
     ///      (GatherForAheadGuard): they were made before it, so they are the frame's own. While
-    ///      the guard is up nothing more is gathered: what the cores collect meanwhile is a later
-    ///      frame's, stays with them (and in ForEachPendingCpuWrite's view), and is applied by
-    ///      the first gather after the guard is lifted.
+    ///      the guard is up, a gathered write that went to a copied page is a later frame's, to a
+    ///      page the frame in flight reads: it is kept (in ForEachPendingCpuWrite's view, and out
+    ///      of the GPU-written ranges at once, so no download lands over it) and applied by the
+    ///      first gather after the guard is lifted. Every other write is applied as before.
     void GatherForApply(std::function<void(PAddr, size_t)>& callback_writes) {
         if (!VideoCommon::AheadGuard::Enabled()) [[likely]] {
             system.GatherGPUDirtyMemory(callback_writes);
@@ -203,8 +204,26 @@ struct GPU::Impl {
         }
         ahead_gathered_writes.clear();
         if (!VideoCommon::AheadGuard::HoldWrites()) {
+            for (const auto& [address, size] : ahead_held_writes) {
+                callback_writes(address, size);
+            }
+            ahead_held_writes.clear();
             system.GatherGPUDirtyMemory(callback_writes);
             VideoCommon::AheadGuard::TakeRedirty(callback_writes);
+            return;
+        }
+        std::vector<std::pair<DAddr, u64>> kept;
+        std::function<void(PAddr, size_t)> split([&](PAddr address, size_t size) {
+            if (VideoCommon::AheadGuard::HasCopy(address, size)) {
+                kept.emplace_back(address, size);
+            } else {
+                callback_writes(address, size);
+            }
+        });
+        system.GatherGPUDirtyMemory(split);
+        if (!kept.empty()) {
+            renderer->ReadRasterizer()->ClaimCpuWrites(kept);
+            ahead_held_writes.insert(ahead_held_writes.end(), kept.begin(), kept.end());
         }
     }
 
@@ -299,12 +318,16 @@ struct GPU::Impl {
         for (auto& manager : system.GetGPUDirtyMemoryManager()) {
             manager.ForEachPending(callback);
         }
-        // EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD=3: the writes gathered at a present and not applied yet.
+        // EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD=3: the writes gathered at a present and not applied yet, and
+        // those kept until a guard is lifted.
         if (VideoCommon::AheadGuard::Mode() == 3) [[unlikely]] {
             std::scoped_lock lock{ahead_gather_mutex};
             for (const auto& [address, size] : ahead_gathered_writes) {
                 callback(address, size);
             }
+            for (const auto& [address, size] : ahead_held_writes) {
+                callback(address, size);
+            }
         }
         // EDEN_UP_L1028_ASYNC_READBACK or EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_DOWNLOAD_LANDING: the gathered writes
         // being applied (GatherAndApply).
@@ -670,8 +693,10 @@ struct GPU::Impl {
     std::vector<const std::vector<std::pair<DAddr, u64>>*> applying_writes;
     std::mutex applying_writes_mutex;
     /// EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD=3: guest writes gathered at a present (GatherForAheadGuard), for the
-    /// next GatherAndApply; the mutex also keeps the two gathers apart.
+    /// next GatherAndApply, and those kept until a guard is lifted; the mutex also keeps the two
+    /// gathers apart.
     std::vector<std::pair<DAddr, u64>> ahead_gathered_writes;
+    std::vector<std::pair<DAddr, u64>> ahead_held_writes;
     std::mutex ahead_gather_mutex;
 
     const bool is_async;
diff --git a/src/video_core/rasterizer_interface.h b/src/video_core/rasterizer_interface.h
index c899bdb..978488c 100644
--- a/src/video_core/rasterizer_interface.h
+++ b/src/video_core/rasterizer_interface.h
@@ -202,6 +202,11 @@ public:
         }
